KNOWNBUG: N5008 [expr.prim.fold] + [temp.variadic]/5 -- a fold expression
`(a + ...)` over a function parameter pack in a MEMBER function template's
body is not expanded when the member is instantiated, so the bare pack
name fails to resolve and the body is dropped ("no body for callee
S::sum"; the call returns nondet).  Root cause: member function template
bodies are prepared by prepare_deferred_method_body's pack-expander,
which -- unlike the free-function-template body expander in
cpp_instantiate_template (which handles cpp_left_fold/cpp_right_fold/
cpp_binary_fold) -- has no fold-expression handling.  The identical fold
in a FREE function template works; the enclosing class need not be a
template.  Minimal (2 logical lines), header-free, g++/clang++
runtime-verified.  Flip to CORE when the member-template body expander
expands fold expressions.
